==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gmh|immer}} (also {{m|gmh|iemer}}, {{m|gmh|imer}}), from {{der|de|goh|iomer|iomēr|always}}. From {{compound|goh|io|mer|alt2=mēr||t1=always|t2=more|nocat=1}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|immer}}, {{cog|nds-de|immer}}, {{m|nds-de|ümmer}}, {{m|nds-de|jümmer}}, {{m|nds-de|jümmers}}, {{cog|enm|a mare}}, {{m|enm|aa mare|t=evermore}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈɪmɐ/}}
* {{audio|de|De-immer.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-immer2.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-immer.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɪmɐ|s=2}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[always]]
## at all times without exception
##: {{ux|de|Irgendwo scheint '''immer''' die Sonne.|The sun is '''always''' shining somewhere.}}
## very often; all the time; [[constantly]]
##: {{ux|de|Er will '''immer''' nur fernsehen.|He just wants to watch telly '''all the time'''.}}
## every time; whenever some precondition is given
##: {{ux|de|Er erzählt '''immer''' dieselbe Geschichte.|He '''always''' tells that same story.}}
# {{lb|de|with [[Appendix:Glossary#comparative|comparative]]}} to a greater degree over time, [[more and more]]
#: {{uxi|de|Es wird '''immer''' kälter.|It's getting colder and colder.}}
# {{lb|de|colloquial|unstressed}} {{n-g|used to emphasize another adverb of time, which itself is stressed}}
#: {{uxi|de|Er kommt '''immer''' nie pünktlich.|He’s never on time.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Ich bin oft '''immer''' sehr vergesslich.|I’m often very forgetful.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Manchmal hab ich '''immer''' das Gefühl, dass...|Sometimes I get the feeling that...}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|at all times}} {{l|de|stets}} {{q|but somewhat uncommon in this sense}}; {{l|de|allzeit}} {{q|dated, poetic}}
* {{sense|very often}} {{l|de|stets}} {{q|formal}}; {{l|de|dauernd}}; {{l|de|ständig}}; {{l|de|immerzu}}
* {{sense|every time}} {{l|de|stets}} {{q|formal}}; {{l|de|[[jedes]] [[Mal]]}}

====Derived terms====
